@doc """
Why a client request failed inside `HTTP` itself. `InvalidUrl` says
the URL cannot be requested, `Parse` carries why the response was
rejected, and `Timeout` says the request passed its time limit.

A network failure is not an `HTTP.Error`. The client functions fail
with `HTTP.Error | Socket.Error | IO.Error | TLSError`, so a refused
connection or a certificate that did not verify keeps its own type.
"""
enum Error
  InvalidUrl(String)
  Parse(Parser.Error)
  Timeout

  @doc """
  Returns a human-readable description of the error.
  """
  fn message(self) -> String
    match self
      Error.InvalidUrl(msg) -> "invalid URL: " <> msg
      Error.Parse(cause) -> "invalid response: " <> cause.message()
      Error.Timeout -> "request timed out"
    end
  end
end
